# Development-only files, kept out of the assembled payload.
#
# tools/build_release.py reads this file when it zips the mod directory that
# `bwsprites mod -external` produced, and matches entries as EXACT relative
# paths (modkit's rule: no prefixes, no globs).  The assembled payload holds
# only manifest.json and the Lua, so nothing here is normally present; the
# entries exist for a hand-built release made *into the repo root* instead.
#
# A version bump means editing the two asset-name guards below.
README.md
CHANGELOG.md

# A guard, not a description of the tree: these are build products, never
# committed (see .gitignore and .github/workflows/release.yml).
BW-Animated-Sprites-1.0.0.zip
BW-Animated-Sprites-1.0.0.modpkg
